        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={(4x+6)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$\n\n${f}^{\u2032}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $g(x)=4x+6$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5}{)}^{\u2032}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{\u2032}(x) & =(4x+6{)}^{\u2032}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={f}^{\u2032}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot (4) \\\\  & =20(4x+6{)}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
